<title>MAURITIUS: Mauritius rupee weakens against dollar.</title>
<headline>Mauritius rupee weakens against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>PORT LOUIS 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mauritian rupee weakened slightly against both dollar and sterling on Tuesday, reflecting international market trends, foreign exchange dealers said.</p>
<p>The rupee was quoted at a commercial mean rate of 21.2905 to the dollar from 21.2405 on Monday, and at 35.6925 to sterling from 35.6525.</p>
<p>Foreign exchange dealers said the rupee's fixing was in line with dollar strengthening in international markets.</p>
<p>--Clifford Vellien ++230 211-9555</p>
</text>
